+++
title = "My CSS Reset"
date = "2025-08-11"
draft = false
tags = ["css"]
+++

```css
*,
*::before,
*::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
* {
  margin: 0;
}
body {
  line-height: 1.5;
}

input,
button,
textarea,
select {
  font: inherit;
}
```
This is the quick-and-dirty CSS reset I use to make my styles look more consistent across browsers. It serves as a nice starting point as I begin styling a new website.

Inspired by [Josh Comeau's](https://www.joshwcomeau.com/) [CSS reset](https://www.joshwcomeau.com/css/custom-css-reset/).

See the OG reset by Eric Meyer -> [CSS Tools: Reset CSS](https://meyerweb.com/eric/tools/css/reset/).

That's all folks.
